Exchanger
_______________________________________________
An Exchanger is a synchronization tool in Java used when two threads want to exchange data with each other.
Both threads meet at a point and swap objects.

Very Simple Example

Two friends meet.

Friend A gives Apple
Friend B gives Orange

They exchange items.

That meeting point = Exchanger

--------------------------------------
In Programming Meaning

Two threads run separately.

When ready:

Thread 1 gives its data
Thread 2 gives its data

Both receive each other’s data.
-----------------------------
Constructor
Exchanger<String> exchanger = new Exchanger<>();


Creates exchanger for String data.
----------------------------------
Main Method
exchange()
String data = exchanger.exchange(myData);


Meaning:

Give your data
Wait for other thread
Receive other thread’s data